The one token in a `set` hook carrying no `=` is a file target, resolved against the
workdir rather than the artifact. The report names it, the artifact keeps only its status, and the
target's existing keys and body survive the write.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-hooks
title: Hooks
summary: Hook-bearing fixture for transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  only: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: noted
            when: the brief is reviewed
            hooks: ["set brief.md reviewed=recorded"]
      noted: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/only/prompt.md --
---
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- fixtures/cwd/run/brief.md --
---
title: Brief
---

Brief body.
-- cmd --
booping transition run/index.md intaking --playbook fx-hooks
booping transition run/index.md noted --playbook fx-hooks
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
created index.md
not-started → intaking
frontmatter: status=intaking
intaking → noted
frontmatter: status=noted
frontmatter brief.md: reviewed=recorded
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/run/brief.md --
---
title: Brief
reviewed: recorded
---

Brief body.
-- expected/cwd/run/index.md --
---
status: noted
---
